    "id": "12114",
    "question": "Where is the liver?",
    "answer": "Left",
    "native_answer_type": "OPEN",
    "category": "Position",
    "delta": 1.0,
    "generalist": "Right side of abdomen.",
    "bard": "The liver is in the upper right quadrant of your abdomen. It's a large, dark organ that sits under your diaphragm and helps filter blood from your digestive system before it enters other organs like the portal vein or hepatic veins.\n\nIn medical terms, this means:\n\n- The liver occupies most of the space on the right side of your abdominal cavity.\n- Its location can be described as being just below the ribcage (intra-abdominal) but above where you would find your stomach and intestines.\n- You might also hear doctors refer to specific parts of the liver by their names: the left lobe, middle lobe, caudate lobe, and right lobe - each with its own unique function within overall liver health.\n\nRemember though, while I've provided some basic information here about where exactly the liver is located physically inside your body, any concerns regarding its condition should always be discussed directly with healthcare professionals who have access to detailed imaging studies such as CT scans for accurate diagnosis and treatment planning purposes."
  },
