    "delta": 0.6666666666666666,
    "generalist": "Right side of abdomen.",
    "bard": "The liver is in the upper right quadrant of your abdomen. It's a large organ that helps filter blood from your digestive system, store energy as glycogen and produce important proteins like albumin and clotting factors.\n\nIn this CT scan image you provided, we can see various structures within the abdominal cavity including what appears to be part of the liver on the left side (which would actually be the patient’s right side due to how medical images are typically displayed). The liver occupies much of the space above the diaphragm and below the ribs; it has an irregular shape but generally looks homogenous without any obvious lesions or abnormalities visible at this slice level.\n\nRemember though, for accurate diagnosis and assessment, such interpretations should always be confirmed by qualified healthcare professionals who have access to full clinical context along with these imaging findings."
  },
